{
  "kanji": "曲",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 曲\ntitle: bend; musical piece\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 曰\nradicalNumber: 73\nonyomi: [キョク]\nkunyomi: [ま.がる, ま.げる, くま]\ndistractors: [田, 用, 画]\n---\n\n# 曲 — bend; musical piece\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 曰 (no. 73) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\nLearn two practical branches: bending or turning in 曲がる まがる, and a piece of music in\n[曲](../words/曲.md) きょく. A musical 曲 may be a song or an instrumental piece.\nThe musical sense is not an instruction to bend something.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** trace an imaginary turning route through the divided box.\nThis is a visual memory aid, not a claim about historical development. The dictionary's indexing\nradical is 曰, distinct from 日.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キョク | on | [曲](../words/曲.md) きょく — piece of music |\n| ま.がる | kun | 曲がる まがる — bend; turn |\n| ま.げる | kun | 曲げる まげる — bend something |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [曲](../words/曲.md) きょく — musical composition; track\n- 曲がる まがる — curve; turn\n- 曲げる まげる — bend something\n\n## Notes\n\n道が曲がる (みちがまがる), \"the road curves,\" describes its course.\n指を曲げる (ゆびをまげる), \"bend a finger,\" names what someone bends.\n[田](田.md), [用](用.md) and [画](画.md) also have divided enclosures; count the vertical lines\nand notice which project beyond the top.\n\nVocabulary: JMdict entries 1239700, 1239730 and 1239740.\n",
